ENV TRIAGE NOTES (why the first bake attempt was garbage — do not repeat):
- ~/LTS root on omarchy still holds this morning's ja-campaign qa-rN.*/
  repair-rN.* files; qa-asr.py's resume carried 1627 settled JA rows into
  the new run and the loop then wrote 1455 JA ids into the IDS file.
  ALWAYS run the loop in a fresh directory with fresh log/ids names.
- bake-repair-loop.sh passes one LANG to generate (--language) AND to
  whisper: generate needs the NAME 'russian' ('ru' = language unsupported);
  whisper accepts the name too. Launch: russian.
- The loop rewrites its IDS file in place; keep a pristine ids copy.
- Remote launch on omarchy: fish shell — backgrounding needs the launcher
  in a script file (bash a2-launch.sh), not an inline `cmd &` over ssh.

